<title>GREECE: Greek retail sales rise 11.5pct yr/yr in Oct.</title>
<headline>Greek retail sales rise 11.5pct yr/yr in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's retail sales rose 11.5 percent year-on-year in October from 7.2 percent in September, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said in a statement.</p>
<p>Foodstuffs rose 5.1 percent, apparel and footwear by 12.3 percent, furniture and household goods by 14.6 percent and miscellaneous by 14.3 percent, it said.</p>
<p>Average sales were up 10.5 percent year-on-year in the period January-October, it said.</p>
<p>    Retail sales	  Oct 96    Sept 96     Oct 95</p>
<p>    Year-on-year(pct)    285.6     254.7	 256.2</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
